e Future 120", "year": 2026, "rank": 87, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "aiq", "title": "Fortune AIQ 75", "year": 2026, "rank": 12, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2026, "rank": 116, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2026, "rank": 43, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "americas-most-innovative-companies", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "year": 2026, "rank": 17, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2025, "rank": 106, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2025, "rank": 43, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "americas-most-innovative-companies", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "year": 2025, "rank": 11, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "100-fastest-growing-companies", "title": "100 Fastest-Growing Companies", "year": 2024, "rank": 42, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2024, "rank": 110, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500--motor-vehicles-parts", "title": "Fortune Sector Leaders: Motor Vehicles and Parts", "year": 2024, "rank": 3, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2024, "rank": 40, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "americas-most-innovative-companies", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "year": 2024, "rank": 11, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2023, "rank": 152, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "americas-most-innovative-companies", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "year": 2023, "rank": 17, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2023, "rank": 50, "itemDescription": "The EV maker has flown up the Fortune 500 since its 2017 debut. Its 51% revenue growth in 2022 boosted it into the Fortune 50, a milestone it reached faster than any other company on this year\u2019s list. Tesla also led all Fortune 500 companies with an annualized 49% 10-year total return to shareholders through 2022.<br />\r\n<ul><br />\r\n \t<li>Tesla slashed prices multiple times in the first few months of 2023 on various models to drive sales volume, but the move squeezed the company\u2019s operating profit margin and dinged its stock. Tesla raised prices again in May 2023.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>In April 2023, Tesla won a lawsuit that had aimed to hold the company\u2019s Autopilot driver-assist software responsible for a crash years prior, but it faced other safety concerns with probes into faulty seat belts and steering wheels on some models.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>Tesla CEO Elon Musk announced his CEO successor at Twitter in May 2023, a signal that he would refocus his energies on Tesla; Tesla shares rose on the news.</li><br />\r\n</ul>"}, {"slug": "100-fastest-growing-companies", "title": "100 Fastest-Growing Companies", "year": 2023, "rank": 2, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2022, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2022, "rank": 242, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2022, "rank": 65, "itemDescription": "<span style=\"font-weight: 400\">The electric car company headed by Elon Musk continued its meteoric rise up the rankings, climbing 35 spots over last year. The company had a blockbuster 2021, bringing in $53.8 billion in revenue, up 70% from 2020, and expanding significantly into key European and Chinese markets. Tesla delivered 936,000 vehicles in 2021, an 87% increase that puts the company at the pinnacle of the global EV industry, with a 14% market share. The company sustained its growth in the early months of 2022, weathering uncertainty and periodic factory shutdowns due to the COVID-19 pandemic in China to deliver 310,048 vehicles in the first quarter, en route to posting record quarterly earnings.</span>"}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2021, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2021, "rank": 392, "itemDescription": "<span data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;Elon Musk\u2019s electric-car company cruised to No. 100 on this year\u2019s list. It\u2019s a big accomplishment for the automaker, which brought in $31.5 billion in sales for its fiscal 2020, a 28% jump over the previous year. Tesla also reported a profit of $721 million in 2020, driven largely by regulatory credits. While Consumer Reports ranked Tesla second to last in its most recent automobile reliability survey, the carmaker still captivates investors\u2014not least because of its recent big bet on Bitcoin. Tesla remains the most valuable automaker in the world with a market cap of nearly $600 billion as of May.&quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:12673,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;10&quot;:2,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;15&quot;:&quot;Calibri, Arial&quot;,&quot;16&quot;:11}\" data-sheets-textstyleruns=\"{&quot;1&quot;:0}\uee10{&quot;1&quot;:312,&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;6&quot;:1}}\uee10{&quot;1&quot;:328}\">Elon Musk\u2019s electric-car company brought in $31.5 billion in sales for its fiscal 2020, a 28% jump over the previous year. Tesla also reported a profit of $721 million in 2020, driven largely by regulatory credits. While Consumer Reports ranked Tesla second to last in its most recent automobile reliability survey, the carmaker still captivates investors\u2014not least because of its recent big bet on Bitcoin. Tesla remains the most valuable automaker in the world with a market cap of nearly $625 billion as of July.</span>"}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2021, "rank": 100, "itemDescription": "<span data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;Elon Musk\u2019s electric-car company cruised to No. 100 on this year\u2019s list. It\u2019s a big accomplishment for the automaker, which brought in $31.5 billion in sales for its fiscal 2020, a 28% jump over the previous year. Tesla also reported a profit of $721 million in 2020, driven largely by regulatory credits. While Consumer Reports ranked Tesla second to last in its most recent automobile reliability survey, the carmaker still captivates investors\u2014not least because of its recent big bet on Bitcoin. Tesla remains the most valuable automaker in the world with a market cap of nearly $600 billion as of May.&quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:12673,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;10&quot;:2,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;15&quot;:&quot;Calibri, Arial&quot;,&quot;16&quot;:11}\" data-sheets-textstyleruns=\"{&quot;1&quot;:0}\uee10{&quot;1&quot;:312,&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;6&quot;:1}}\uee10{&quot;1&quot;:328}\">Elon Musk\u2019s electric-car company cruised to No. 100 on this year\u2019s list. It\u2019s a big accomplishment for the automaker, which brought in $31.5 billion in sales for its fiscal 2020, a 28% jump over the previous year. Tesla also reported a profit of $721 million in 2020, driven largely by regulatory credits. While Consumer Reports ranked Tesla second to last in its most recent automobile reliability survey, the carmaker still captivates investors\u2014not least because of its recent big bet on Bitcoin. Tesla remains the most valuable automaker in the world with a market cap of nearly $600 billion as of May.</span>"}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2020, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "future", "title": "The Future 50", "year": 2020, "rank": 18, "itemDescription": "<p class=\"p1\">Elon Musk\u2019s EV and battery manufacturer leaps up the ranking as it becomes one of the world\u2019s most valuable companies. Why such potential? Furious expansion of its global manufacturing capacity should allow Tesla to begin producing greater volumes of cars, thus improving cash flow and justifying its eye-watering valuation, and perhaps even dragging the auto industry into a fossil\u00a0fuel\u2013less future. (See our <a href=\"https://fortune.com/longform/elon-musk-ceo-tesla-spacex-2020-businessperson-of-the-year/\">profile of Musk</a> in this issue.)</p>"}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2020, "rank": 124, "itemDescription": "Elon Musk's electric-car company, which jumps up 20 spots on this year's <em>Fortune</em> 500, unveiled its Cybertruck late last year with production planned for late 2021."}, {"slug": "future", "title": "The Future 50", "year": 2019, "rank": 48, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2019, "rank": 144, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "future", "title": "The Future 50", "year": 2018, "rank": 48, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2018, "rank": 260, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "future", "title": "The Future 50", "year": 2017, "rank": 2, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2017, "rank": 383, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2016, "rank": 588, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "change-the-world", "title": "Change the World", "year": 2016, "rank": 50, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2015, "rank": 717, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2014, "rank": 965, "itemDescription": ""}]}